@startuml
!pragma layout smetana

title Confirmation lifecycle

skinparam state {
    BackgroundColor #E3F0DC
    BorderColor #4C7A44
    FontColor #1A1A1E
    AttributeFontColor #3A3A3E
    ArrowColor #4C7A44
    ArrowFontColor #1A1A1E
    StartColor #4C7A44
    EndColor #4C7A44
}
skinparam note {
    BackgroundColor #FBF3D3
    BorderColor #C9A227
    FontColor #1A1A1E
}
skinparam BackgroundColor white
skinparam DefaultFontColor #1A1A1E

state "not required" as NotRequired #EFEFEF ##[bold]888888
state "unconfirmed" as Unconfirmed
state "queried" as Queried
state "affirmed" as Affirmed
state "confirmed" as Confirmed

NotRequired : Nobody to agree terms with
Unconfirmed : Terms not yet agreed
Queried : The two records differ
Affirmed : Both sides agree the terms
Confirmed : Binding written record

[*] --> NotRequired : Book [no counterparty]
[*] --> Unconfirmed : Book [faces a counterparty]
Unconfirmed --> Queried : Query
Unconfirmed --> Affirmed : Affirm
Queried --> Affirmed : Resolve
Affirmed --> Confirmed : Confirm
Confirmed --> Unconfirmed : Amend

note right of Confirmed
  Confirmed as of an external version.
  A confirmable amendment moves that
  version and returns the trade to
  unconfirmed.
end note

note left of Unconfirmed
  An unconfirmed trade is a counterparty
  risk: the terms are not enforceable in
  the form the parties agreed. It is not
  a reason to withhold the trade from
  risk and P&L.
end note

note bottom of Affirmed
  No state here is terminal. When the
  trade expires or is cancelled this
  lifecycle stops, and the status keeps
  its last value, which still records
  whether the trade was ever confirmed.
end note

note right of NotRequired
  The default. An intra-entity transfer,
  a test booking or a hypothetical stays
  here for its whole life. Every trade
  has a status; none is null.
end note

@enduml
